"tiny k" <kdlittle88@yahoo.com> writes:
> Anyone know how many XP is needed for a pet's experience levels?

They don't gain XP; they gain (max) HP directly. They need 5 HP to
reach ML 1, then 9 HP for ML 2, 17 for ML 3, ((n-1)*8)+1 HP for ML n.
The cap on level gain through experience is (base level)*3/2.

> Also, what do they get then they gain a new level?  I know they get hp,
> but how many?

They gain being a higher level, with all that implies (to-hit bonus
and saving throw modifier, primarily), and may grow to a larger or more
senior form of that monster if one exists (generally getting them
better attacks, possibly better natural speed and AC).

> Also I think they only get 1 xp per monster killed, but does that
> ever change?

Any monster killing another monster of level ML will get d(ML+1) HP
(though no more than needed to reach the next level).

